[First Time]

-> Wallpaper Changes
-> meowterialyou --reapply happens
-> Get current wallpaper from .config/background
-> Hash the image and store somewhere
-> Convert to color scheme if specified and hash the converted image
-> Now we have two hashes, one for the original image and one for the converted image
-> MaterialYou colors generate from converted image if converted image exists, else from original image
-> Set wallpaper to converted image if converted image exists, else to original image

Now setting wallpaper to converted image triggers reapply again probably.

-> meowterialyou --reapply happens again
-> Get current wallpaper (which is likely converted) from .config/background
-> Hash and compare with previous hash of converted
-> If they match, skip the rest of the process
